# Heavy env, rebuilt by bin/setup-tts-env.sh
.venv-tts/
# Isolated eval-only env for the Chatterbox-Flash benchmark (2026-08-08).
# Never touches .venv-tts; safe to delete once the bake-off is decided.
.venv-flash/
# Live client data — never in git
assets/hot-context.md
assets/.brain-session-id
assets/turn-timings.jsonl
assets/whisper-server.log
# Rendered audio — regenerable from the frozen reference + RECIPE
assets/phrases/
assets/earcon-ack.wav

# Voice harvest (bin/harvest-voice.py) — Joe's real question/answer content,
# client names, deal specifics. Never in git (PII rule, ORDER 42). The seed
# file, mined questions, replies, sentence splits, and training corpus are
# all local-only and regenerable/re-mineable from Joe's own account export.
assets/harvest-curated-seed.json
assets/harvest-questions.json
assets/harvest-questions-curated.json
assets/harvest-replies.jsonl
assets/harvest-sentences.jsonl
assets/harvest-frames.txt
assets/harvest-factual.txt
assets/harvest-corpus/
assets/harvest-render-progress.json
# Sensitive-tier: Joe's raw Claude export is INPUT to the harvest, never an
# artifact of it. A subagent copied it in here once (2026-08-08, flagged by
# the security layer); this makes a repeat un-committable.
assets/source-exports/
**/conversations.json
assets/harvest-*.json
assets/harvest-*.jsonl
assets/harvest-*.txt
assets/harvest-corpus/
assets/.harvest-brain-session-id
# The qwen eval env. Every sibling venv above has a rule; this one was named
# only in a COMMENT on line 7, so 8,244 files / 663MB landed in git on
# 2026-08-09 (commit 6871583) and made the branch unpushable — one blob,
# mlx.metallib, is 155MB against GitHub's 100MB hard limit.
.venv-qwen/
